Step 1 — Create ASP.NET Core Project
1. Open Visual Studio 2019.
2. Click Create a new project.
3. Select ASP.NET Core Web Application.
4. Click Next.
5. Project Name:
StudentManagement

6. Click Create.
7. Select:
ASP.NET Core Web Application (Model-View-Controller)

8. Click Create.     Practical 2(1)
Step 2 — Add Test Project
1. Right-click the Solution.
2. Select:
Add → New Project

3. Search:
xUnit Test Project (.NET Core)

4. Select it.
5. Click Next.
6. Project Name:
StudentManagement.Tests

7. Click Create.
You should now have:
StudentManagement
StudentManagement.Tests

    Practical 2(1)
Step 3 — Add Project Reference
1. Right-click:
StudentManagement.Tests

2. Select:
Add → Project Reference

3. Tick:
StudentManagement

4. Click OK.     Practical 2(1)
Step 4 — Install Required Packages
Right-click:
StudentManagement.Tests

Select:
Manage NuGet Packages
Install these three:
xunit
xunit.runner.visualstudio
Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk

    Practical 2(1)
Step 5 — Create Calculator Class
In the StudentManagement project:
1. Right-click the project.
2. Select:
Add → Class

3. Name it:
Calculator.cs

4. Add:
namespace StudentManagement
{
    public class Calculator
    {
        public int Add(int a, int b)
        {
            return a + b;
        }

        public int Multiply(int a, int b)
        {
            return a * b;
        }
    }
}

    Practical 2(1)
Step 6 — Create Test Class
Inside:
StudentManagement.Tests

1. Right-click the project.
2. Select:
Add → Class

3. Name it:
CalculatorTests.cs

4. Add:
using Xunit;
using StudentManagement;

namespace StudentManagementTests
{
    public class CalculatorTests
    {
        [Fact]
        public void Add_TwoNumbers_ReturnsSum()
        {
            Calculator c = new Calculator();

            int result = c.Add(10, 20);

            Assert.Equal(30, result);
        }
    }
}

    Practical 2(1)
Step 7 — Run the Test
1. Go to:
Test → Test Explorer

2. Click:
Run All
Step 8 — Expected Output
You should get:
Passed: 1
Failed: 0
Skipped: 0

The test should have a green check mark.     Practical 2(1)
